<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n109445" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑποτύπ-ωσις</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῠ]</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>, ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>sketch, outline,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Str.
				2.5.18
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				2.12
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Anon.
			</span></i> Lond.<i><span class="en">
				7.17
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hermog.
				<u>Prog.</u>
				6
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				7.128
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑ. ἕνεκα συγγράμματος</span>
			<i>draft</i> for a book, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				15.760
			</span></i>; as Empiric term, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				8.709
			</span></i>, al.; opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξεργασία,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plot.
				6.3.7
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπογραφάς τε καὶ
			ὑποτυπώσεις,</span> opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅρους,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>Stoic.</u>
				2.76
			</span></i>: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ Ὑποτυπώσεις</span> was the
			name given by Sextus Empiricus to his <u>Outlines</u> of the
			Pyrrhonic Philosophy, cf. <i><span class="en">
				D.L.
				9.78
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
			</span></i><i>Libr. Propr.Praef.</i>: Proclus calls one of his works
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ ὑ. τῶν ἀστρονομικῶν ὑποθέσεων,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>Hyp.</u>
				7.50
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>model, pattern,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>1 Ep.Ti.</u>
				1.16
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>2 Ep.Ti.</u>
				1.13
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς ὑποτύπωσιν ἀρετῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>Mus.</u>
					p.77
				</span></i>
			 K. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> a Rhet.
			figure, <i>by which a matter was vividly sketched in words,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Quint.
				<u>Inst.</u>
				9.2.40
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
